\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil yields fall on bets of interest rate cut\b0\par\par\uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2012\par 17:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso hits 6-month high on US data then sags\par \par \uc2 * Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fight real's appreciation\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso slips 0.35 pct, Brazil real drops 0.61 pct\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Danielle Fonseca and Jean Arce\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Oct 5 (Reuters) - Yields on Brazil's interest rate futures fell sharply on Friday after comments from a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official pushed investors to bet that policymakers will cut interest rates next week.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, Brazil's real fell after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fight recent gains while \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso whipsawed, surging to a six-month high on a drop in the U.S. unemployment rate, before ending weaker.\par \par \uc2 Bets on a benchmark interest rate cut in Brazil were already on the rise this week, but they increased on Friday after a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director suggested additional monetary easing might be needed to stimulate the economy.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the interest-rate contract maturing January 2013 <0#2DIJ:>, the most traded at the Sao Paulo exchange, fell 9 basis points to 7.092 percent.\par \par \uc2 Luiz Awazu Pereira, a voting member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee, said after markets closed on Thursday that a prolonged period of weak global growth would make it crucial for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to "calibrate" its monetary policy in order to accelerate growth.\par \par \uc2 "Markets bought into what Awazu said yesterday," said Paulo Nepomucemo, a fixed-income strategist at Coinvalores brokerage in Sao Paulo. "The view that the current monetary easing cycle is still not over gained traction."\par \par \uc2 Brazil has slashed its benchmark rate by 500 bps since last August to 7.50 percent in a bid to fight a slowdown in Latin America's biggest economy.\par \par \uc2 Disappointing Brazilian industrial production data for August this week began to stoke bets of more monetary stimulus.\par \par \uc2 Driving early gains in the Mexican peso, the U.S. Labor Department said the U.S. jobless rate fell to 7.8 percent in September, its lowest in nearly four years.\par \par \uc2 The data initially backed hopes that U.S. demand for Mexican exports would hold up despite a global economic slowdown, but investors soon turned their focus to next week and concerns that earnings from U.S. companies could look weak.\par \par \uc2 A meeting of euro zone finance ministers next week could also bring concerns about Europe's debt crisis back into focus for the market, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "People took advantage of the morning's gains to take profits and prepare for what is coming next week," said Jorge Gordillo, an analyst at CI Banco in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso rallied early in the session pushing the cost of dollars in pesos through support at the 12.70 level to touch its strongest intraday level since late March.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversed direction to lose 0.35 percent to 12.79 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The focus will be Europe again next week, and so it will be difficult to get to levels stronger that 12.70," Gordillo said.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil the real lost 0.61 percent to 2.0298 per dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the sale of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivative contracts designed to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It was the first swap sale since Sept. 17, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to offset the impact of the U.S. Federal Reserve's stimulus policies.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian policy makers have pledged to use all the instruments available to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a level that benefits exporters.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the real gained past that level of 2.02, triggering the alarm. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made it clear that it will not allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen past 2 per dollar," said Jaime Ferreira, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Intercam brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2200 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             daily %  year-to-\par                                      change     ate %\par                            Latest              change\par Brazil real                  2.0298     -0.61     -7.95\par                                              \par Mexico peso                 12.7855     -0.32      9.26\par                                              \par Argentina peso*              6.1600      0.49    -23.21\par                                              \par Chile peso                 473.3000     -0.17      9.72\par                                              \par Colombia peso            1,796.1000     -0.05      7.92\par                                              \par Peru sol                     2.5890      0.15      4.17\par                                              \par * Argentine peso's rate between         