\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile peso slumps on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 820 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2012\par 20:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chile cenbank president doesn't rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Colombia says will keep up dollar purchases\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso falls 0.31 pct; Brazil real up 0.28 pct\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Moises Avila and Jean Arce\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO/MEXICO CITY, Sept 28 (Reuters) - Chile's peso slumped by the most in seven weeks on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it could act to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, while Colombia pledged to keep buying dollars in its market to fight peso strength.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso lost nearly 0.8 percent to change hands at 474.60 per U.S. dollar after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Rodrigo Vergara said policymakers may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  during "exceptional periods" in which the exchange rate is significantly out of line with fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 The move by Chile pushed it closer to the stance of policymakers in Brazil, Colombia and Peru who have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to fight dollar inflows that have lifted their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and hurt exporters.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments weakened the peso because they leave the door open for a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The market isn't just speculating about the possibility of dollar purchases, but also bank deposit requirements," said Rodrigo Sarria, a trader at Celfin Capital in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 The peso has gained more than 9 percent so far this year, making it the second strongest performer among the 152 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Stimulus measures announced by the U.S. Federal Reserve and the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosted Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this quarter. The measures are expected to drive down yields on U.S. and European fixed-income instruments, making emerging market assets more attractive.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso gained 5.5 percent against the dollar in the third quarter, while Mexico's peso firmed 4.5 percent. Brazil's real shed 0.8 percent against the greenback in the quarter after \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its benchmark interest rate steady on Friday, and it pledged to extend daily dollar purchases to keep a lid on the peso.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would buy at least $3 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market via auctions from Oct. 1 through March 29, 2013, to take pressure off the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Colombia peso slipped 0.1 percent on Friday, bringing its decline for the quarter to 0.9 percent, hurt by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso lost a modest 0.31 percent to trade at 12.8660 per dollar as concerns about Spain made investors cautious about taking risks in emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 A stress test on Spanish banks showed the institutions need a total of 59.3 billion euros in extra capital, but uncertainty persisted about whether Spain will ask for a bailout that would let the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  begin buying its bonds.\par \par \uc2 "We could see a whole to wave of pressure related to Spain," said Jorge Gordillo, an analyst at CI Banco in Mexico City, saying that concerns about Spain could weigh on the peso in the coming week. "We think that it will be in October when Spain will ask (for a bailout), and if this happens the peso and stock markets are going to take it well."\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2  analysts said the Mexican peso could outperform its emerging market peers in Latin America and Asia because its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  research published on Friday said emerging market attempts to stem capital inflows during the last round of Fed easing had a limited effect in the longer term.\par \par \uc2 Steps pursued by countries such as Brazil, Chile and Colombia, including new taxes on investment, higher bank reserve requirements and tariff reforms, may even make investors see them as a riskier bet, the research paper said.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real decoupled from the rest of the market, rising 0.28 percent to 2.0255 per dollar, as investors tried to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's closing rate at the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian policymakers have pledged to move aggressively to offset expected capital inflows from the easy monetary conditions in the developed world.\par \par \uc2 A senior government official recently told Reuters that Brazil will defend the level of 2 reais per dollar "like a wall."\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2100 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             daily %  year-to-\par                                      change     ate %\par                            Latest              change\par Brazil real                  2.0255      0.28     -7.75\par                                              \par Mexico peso                 12.8660     -0.31      8.58\par                                              \par Argentina peso*              6.2800      0.32    -24.68\par                                              \par Chile peso                 474.6000     -0.76      9.42\par                                              \par Colombia peso            1,800.3000     -0.10      7.67\par                                              \par Peru sol                     2.5980     -0.08      3.81\par                                              \par * Argentine peso's rate between                        \par brokerages                                     \par                                                      \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Natalia Cacioli in Sao Paulo; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama, Gary Crosse and Leslie Adler)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | M | RBN | NAT | C | E | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121001e89s0018x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
