\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Weak global outlook weighs on Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 537 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2012\par 18:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * U.S. jobless claims further pressure Mexican peso\par \par \uc2  * \uc2 Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds off \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for 3rd day\par \par \uc2  * Brazil real dip 0.17 pct; \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso nearly flat \par \par \uc2 (Adds comment, updates prices)\par \par \uc2  By Natalia Cacioli\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, Sept 20 (Reuters) - Major Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were flat to weaker on Thursday as weak manufacturing data in China, Europe, and the United States weighed on prospects for the region's exports.\par \par \uc2  Investors were particularly worried about data indicating the Chinese economy continues to lose momentum. China is the largest consumer of Latin American exports, and its economic slowdown could moderate U.S. dollar inflows to the region that are expected following newly announced U.S. monetary stimulus measures. \par \par \uc2  The Mexican peso was largely unchanged at 12.87 per dollar, off 0.04 percent and also pressured by data showing U.S. new claims for jobless benefits held near two-month highs in the latest week. The United States is Mexico's main trading partner.\par \par \uc2  Thursday marked the fourth consecutive session of losses for the peso, which rallied last week after the U.S. Federal Reserve\par \par \uc2 announced a third round of monetary stimulus.\par \par \uc2  "We can't expect the economic reports  ... to be positive as soon as the stimulus was announced. If the worry was that the majority of countries would slow down, well that is going to continue," said Jorge Gordillo, an economist at CI Banco in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2  "As there's no news to back up the enthusiasm we saw in the previous two weeks, the economic data takes on greater importance."\par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real  Brazil slipped 0.17 pct to 2.0220 reales per dollar at the local close on reduced volatility after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2  Brazilian policymakers sold about $5.7 billion worth of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps last week and on Monday to offset the appreciation trend stoked by the U.S. monetary stimulus. The bank has refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since then, but it is widely expected to act again if the real firms significantly.\par \par \uc2  "As the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , investors stop making bets because they know there will be market interference. Volatility falls, volumes dwindle and the number of market players decline as a result," said Ures Folchini, a treasury vice president at \uc2 WestLB\uc2  bank in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2  "Why would you invest in an asset if prices will not change? There are more interesting options such as interest-rate futures and stocks," he added.\par \par \uc2  Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2130 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             daily %  year-to-\par                                      change     ate %\par                            Latest              change\par Brazil real                  2.0205      0.25     -7.52\par                                              \par Mexico peso                 12.8700     -0.04      8.54\par                                              \par Argentina peso*              6.3000      0.16    -24.92\par                                              \par Chile peso                 470.2000      0.09     10.44\par                                              \par Colombia peso            1,793.6500      0.19      8.07\par                                              \par Peru sol                     2.6020     -0.08      3.65\par                                              \par * Argentine peso's rate between                        \par brokerages                                     \par                                                      \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Writing by Walter Brandimarte; Editing by Leslie Adler)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (walter.brandimarte@thomsonreuters.com; +55 21 2223 7149;\par Reuters Messaging:\par walter.brandimarte.thomsonreuters.com@reuters.net)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | M | RBN | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120923e89k0007k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
