\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1-Fed's QE3 stirs LatAm differences over  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 911 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2012\par 00:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Brazil restarts \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Fed\par \par \uc2  * Speculation that Chile, Colombia could follow\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's QE3 enthusiasm stands out from crowd \par \par \uc2  By Krista Hughes and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2  MEXICO CITY, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The U.S. Federal Reserve's latest round of stimulus spotlights  a gulf between Mexico and its Latin American neighbors as the region girds itself for a likely revival of the "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war."\par \par \uc2  While Mexico embraced the Fed's decision to start a third round of bond-buying, Brazil vowed to unleash an arsenal of new measures to combat what it fears could be a sharp appreciation in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A stronger real could not come at a worse time for Brazil, which is battling slowing growth with a raft of measures to boost the domestic economy. This contrasts with Mexico, which is growing roughly twice as quickly as its rival and has been fretting about a weak peso pushing up prices. Close links to the United States give it a big stake in stronger U.S. growth.\par \par \uc2  "Mexico is clearly one of the few countries in Latin America where you don't have any resistance to peso strength, and you are unlikely to do so, because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  prefers a hands-off attitude," said Clyde Wardle, a strategist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in New York. "That does set Mexico apart."\par \par \uc2  Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged to new highs after the Fed's news, with Chile's peso hitting a one-year high against the U.S. dollar and Mexico's rising to a five-month peak on bets that yield-seeking investors will flood to the region, driving asset prices higher.\par \par \uc2  During the Fed's second round of bond buying in late 2010 and the first half of 2011, a rush of capital pushed the Brazilian real up 12 percent against the dollar while the Mexican and Chilean pesos both gained 8 percent.\par \par \uc2  Economists said a fresh round of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the cards, with Brazil kicking off o n F riday with two \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two hours. Speculation is mounting about increased efforts in Chile and Colombia as well.\par \par \uc2  South American officials, worried that a rise in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will price their exports out of the market and drag on growth, have a history of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains.\par \par \uc2  But in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 , policymakers face a different dynamic as the peso - one of the most liquid emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and often used as a hedge for emerging market risk - has weakened about 30 percent since before the financial crisis.\par \par \uc2  Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Agustin Carstens told Reuters the Fed's new bond buying program, dubbed QE3, would help the economy, giving no sign policymakers would try to stem the peso's rise. \par \par \uc2  In fact, Carstens said the stronger peso would help limit inflation by making imported goods cheaper - a much-needed break for the \uc2 Banco de Mexico\uc2 , which is confronting a spike in inflation to its highest level in more than two years due to fresh food prices. \par \par \uc2  MEXICO AT ODDS\par \par \uc2  Mexico's laissez-faire stance will put it in a different class from Latin American counterparts that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, like Brazil, which also fears competition from Asian powerhouse China and its yuan.\par \par \uc2  Countries that keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  cheap will face higher prices for imported goods at the same time a flush of cheap money probably drives commodity prices higher, economists said.\par \par \uc2  Although price pressures are subdued in Chile, Colombia and Peru - meaning their central banks may not worry too much about the downside of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - inflation accelerated to 5.24 percent in Brazil last month.\par \par \uc2  "QE3 will end up having two different kinds of effects on inflation," said \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  economist Nader Nazmi. \par \par \uc2  "In countries that fight against appreciation... the price of commodities will increase. This could lead to higher inflation in countries that do not allow their exchange rate to appreciate."\par \par \uc2  Reacting to higher inflation by raising interest rates would make \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  even more expensive, a policy Catch-22 that the region faced during the Fed's previous stimulus, when Brazilian Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2  coined the term "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war."\par \par \uc2  The phrase has been adopted by officials in Colombia, whose peso has been the fourth-biggest gainer worldwide this year, firming 7 percent since January despite back-to-back interest rate cuts. The peso rose 0.4 percent on Friday.  \par \par \uc2  "This shows that we should not remain silent in Colombia and that we will have to respond to these kinds of decisions from the United States," Finance Minister Mauricio Cardenas said.\par \par \uc2  Chile's Finance Minister Felipe Larrain had said even before the Fed's Thursday announcement that the country was worried about another round of stimulus, and the peso is approaching levels that have sparked \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past. \par \par \uc2  "These levels for the peso are a concern for authorities. Although we don't expect imminent action, such as an outright \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we do expect to see in the short-term, over the next 30 days, verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  or announcements that try to contain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation," said Ruben Catalan, senior analyst at Bci in Santiago.     \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Anthony Esposito in Santiago; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 US-FED/LATAM (WRAPUP 1) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | NAT | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNA | RNP | DNP | PTD | SXNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120914e89e001dh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
