\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  little changed on China caution\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2012\par 00:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Aug 10 (Reuters) - The Chilean peso dropped on Friday after weak Chinese export numbers signaled a slowing global economy, but \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Brazil and Mexico were little changed as investors considered the possibility of stimulus measures in China.\par \par \uc2 Poor economic data in China had driven emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher on Thursday as they increased expectations the Chinese government would soon launch measures to stimulate the economy.\par \par \uc2 But additional data on Friday showing that Chinese exports rose just 1 percent in July from a year ago shocked investors, especially those in emerging economies, which rely on China as a key destination for their commodity exports.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso led losses in Latin America, falling 0.9 percent to 478.90 per data, as the Chinese data weighed on prospects for prices of copper, Chile's main export product.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real gained 0.1 percent, however, in its fourth consecutive session of gains.\par \par \uc2 The market could soon test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's willingness to defend the level of 2 reais per dollar, considered by investors as an informal floor to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "The real may slowly fall to the level of 2 per dollar, but there is not room for it to strengthen much further, considering the obstacles imposed by the government," said Jose Carlos Amado, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with Renascenca brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 The real has been trading in a narrow range of 2.0 to 2.1 per dollar since the beginning of July, under the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso gained 0.1 percent to 13.0850 per greenback, closing the week with gains of about 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2200 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          daily %    YTD %\par                                   change   change\par                          Latest           \par Brazil real                2.0145     0.07    -7.25\par                                           \par Mexico peso               13.0850     0.13     6.76\par                                           \par Argentina peso*            6.2400     0.32   -24.20\par                                           \par Chile peso               478.9000    -0.86     8.44\par                                           \par Colombia peso          1,791.0000    -0.17     8.23\par                                           \par Peru sol                   2.6160     0.00     3.10\par                                           \par * Argentine peso's rate between                    \par brokerages                                  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting By Walter Brandimarte; Editing by Kenneth Barry)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120813e88a0017u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
