\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  slip on US data, European woes\b0\par\par\uc2 537 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2012\par 18:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts; updates numbers, adds details)\par \par \uc2 * US retail sales down for 2nd straight month, spur stimulus talk\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real off 0.3 pct, Mexico peso flat\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, June 13 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Wednesday as disappointing U.S. economic data and lingering fears about the euro zone debt crisis sapped investor sentiment.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real slipped 0.29 percent to 2.0706 per dollar, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed weaker than the 2.05 level that triggered a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Monday. In \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso fell to 14.0300 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The euro zone's uncertain future ahead of a Greek election on Sunday, rising concerns about a banking crisis in Spain that has hiked bond yields and fears that Italy may be the next victim in Europe's debt crisis kept market players on edge.\par \par \uc2 "A little weaker U.S. data, Spanish yields still pressured against the backdrop of what we have this weekend, it's hard to think that a lot of peso long (positions) are coming out of the wood work. The same for Brazil," said Bret Rosen, Latin American strategist at Standard Chartered in New York.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, comments by Finance Minister Guido Mantega had given the real an early boost on hopes the government would remove measures originally intended to curb excess dollar inflows. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped by close with some traders cautious on Europe and others betting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slips further.\par \par \uc2 "In the afternoon investors seemed to be squaring positions or hedging themselves for (possible losses) tomorrow morning," said a trader at brokerage Renascenca.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with O Globo daily, Mantega said "some of those (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) measures could be reviewed in due time." He specifically mentioned a recent imposition of a 6 percent financial tax on dollar loans taken by Brazilian companies and banks abroad with a maturity of up to five years.\par \par \uc2 A second consecutive month of falling U.S. retail sales hurt\par \par \uc2 the Mexican peso, which lost 0.45 percent. The United States is Mexico's largest trading partner.\par \par \uc2 Still, the Chilean peso rose 0.5 percent to 502.20 per dollar as the weak data added to expectations of another round of U.S. monetary stimulus that would maintain dollars flowing into emerging market economies.\par \par \uc2 "We just saw lower-than-expected U.S. economic data, which increase the possibility of further stimulus measures," said Rodrigo Sarria, a trader with Celfin Capital in Santiago. "In the very short term, we could test the level of 500 per dollar."\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices from Reuters at 2050 GMT: \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            daily pct\par                                       change\par                            Latest  \par Brazil real                  2.0706      -0.29\par                                    \par Mexico peso                 14.0300      -0.45\par                                    \par Argentina peso*              5.8700       0.85\par                                    \par Chile peso                 502.2000       0.32\par    