\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Mexico ready to handle peso volatility-Carstens\b0\par\par\uc2 730 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2012\par 21:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Carstens says Mexico equipped for peso swings\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drops to more than three-year low\par \par \uc2 * Traders speculate about ad hoc \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments and background)\par \par \uc2 By Isela Serrano and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 CANCUN, Mexico/MEXICO CITY, June 1 (Reuters) - Mexico is well prepared to deal with peso volatility, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Agustin Carstens said on Friday, fanning speculation that the bank could unleash more firepower to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A precipitous drop in Mexico's peso to a more than three-year low is testing policymakers' commitment to a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  although recent moves fall well short of the swings seen in late 2008 following the collapse of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Carstens said Mexico was committed to its flexible exchange rate and said Latin America's second-biggest economy would have to live with swings in the peso, but he also invoked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's discretion to throw its weight into the market if needed.\par \par \uc2 "In any case we are well equipped to face volatility in the case that we need to use resources to stabilize the market," Carstens said at an event in Cancun.\par \par \uc2 "We are ... believers that we should let the exchange rate function to the greatest degree possible ... and introduce mechanisms that soften the movements, above all when markets are not operating fully," he said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  has eschewed the ad hoc market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen in Brazil, India and Indonesia and instead relies on a program where a large dip automatically triggers an auction of $400 million.\par \par \uc2 Its last round of ad hoc \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  was triggered in October 2008 when the peso dropped 6 percent in a single day to hit its lowest level in 16 years amid tight liquidity conditions.\par \par \uc2 The fall on Friday took Mexico's peso down as much as 2 percent to hit its weakest since March 2009, adding to a slump of more than 9 percent in May.\par \par \uc2 MARKET CHATTER\par \par \uc2 A rebound in the euro helped curb the peso's losses and drag it into positive territory, but traders said Carstens' comments fueled talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could alter its current dollar auction mechanism and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively to support the peso, which gained 0.39 percent to 13.2950 per dollar after he spoke.\par \par \uc2 "You have got to suspect they are going to come in and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point in time, and I think that's essentially what you see in the possible turnaround," said Enrique Alvarez, an analyst at IDEAglobal in New York.\par \par \uc2 A poll by Reuters of 14 traders estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take new measures if the peso slumps to a range of 14.70 per dollar to 15.30 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "We are not getting too far from the point where they would start thinking about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Neil Shearing, an emerging markets economist at London-based Capital Economics.\par \par \uc2 Still, top policymakers this week said Mexico was not worried by the peso's drop and insisted they were happy with the existing dollar auction framework, considered one of the most market-friendly forms of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around.\par \par \uc2 Carstens and Finance Minister Jose Antonio Meade both told Reuters this week that they were confident the peso would rebound once global fears about Europe's debt crisis ease.\par \par \uc2 Other analysts were more skeptical that \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  would move to change its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy.\par \par \uc2 "I do not expect to see additional measures anytime soon," said Alonso Cervera, an economist at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 . "This volatility is only temporary."\par \par \uc2 Mexico's auction program offers up to $400 million at three scheduled auctions a day whenever the peso declines by at least 2 percent against the dollar compared with the previous day's fix price, a mid-session reference price.\par \par \uc2 While the program was revived late last year, an auction had not been triggered until last week, the first dollar sale since late 2009.\par \par \uc2 Another sale was triggered on Thursday after a poll showed a surge in support for the leftist presidential candidate, casting doubt on bets that the pro-market front-runner had a victory in the bag for a July 1 vote.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Isela Serrano, Jean Arce and Rachel Uranga; Editing by James Dalgleish and Kenneth Barry)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120601e861001bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
