\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico's Peso At Weakest Close In 6 Months On Spain Worries\b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2012\par 22:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Peso closes at MXN14.1465 to the U.S. dollar, weakest in six months\par \par \uc2 -- Spanish debt yields, bank health drive latest round of risk selling\par \par \uc2 -- Losses not enough to trigger further dollar sales\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Anthony Harrup \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso fell sharply against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, closing at its weakest level this year as fears about the euro zone switched from Greece to Spain, pummeling the euro and emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  along with it.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso was quoted closing in Mexico City at MXN14.1465 to the dollar, according to Infosel, compared with MXN13.8795 at the close Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso's slide to its weakest close in six months didn't go far enough to prompt dollar sales under the 2% rule at the Bank of Mexico's daily auctions. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  auctions up to $400 million at a minimum price that is 2% above the previous day's fix. The trigger price for dollar sales Wednesday was MXN14.1952.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Mexico sold $258 million last week when the peso moved above MXN14 to the dollar for the first time since late November. The sale had little effect on Mexico's foreign reserves, which rose last week to $154.3 billion, boosted by $1 billion in oil dollars from state monopoly \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleos Mexicanos\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The role of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the most sensitive asset to global volatility is confirmed, as risk aversion last week triggered the first dollar-sale auction by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  commission since the mechanism was reintroduced in November 2011," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  unit Banamex said in a report. "Nevertheless, peso depreciation against the USD has not led to significant underperformance in comparison to other [emerging market] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banamex said further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Mexico\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are "very likely" in coming weeks, as the euro crisis continues.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greek opinion polls at the weekend showing voter support for a pro-euro party over one that opposes the bailout led to a two-day respite for the peso, but rising borrowing costs in Spain and worries about the health of Spain's banks put the euro zone back at the forefront of investor concerns Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Mexico Governor Agustin Carstens said earlier this month that the peso is weaker than it should be, given the country's strong economic fundamentals, and that the exchange rate should come down once the market turbulence subsides.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mexican monetary and financial authorities don't target specific levels for the peso, insisting that their main concern is an orderly market in which there is adequate liquidity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Anthony Harrup, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5980-5176, anthony.harrup@dowjones.com [ 30-05-12 2019GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1027 1852   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120530e85u0017p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
