\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real rallies past 2/dlr,  \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso falls\b0\par\par\uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2012\par 17:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Brazil gov't sources on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 * Brazil cenbank offers \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps when real traded flat\par \par \uc2 * Real trades below 2/dlr for first time since May 15\par \par \uc2 * Peru cenbank sells dollars for 1st time since Oct. 2011\par \par \uc2 * Real ends 1.7 pct higher, Mexican peso weakens 0.16 pct\par \par \uc2 By Natalia Cacioli\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, May 25 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real on Friday rallied through the level of 2 per dollar for the first time in 10 days as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped up its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but other Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on European debt fears.\par \par \uc2 In a more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday offered to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps early in the session, when the real was practically flat from Thursday's close.\par \par \uc2 The strategy left many investors wondering whether policymakers were uncomfortable with the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but two government sources told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were only aimed at limiting volatility after the real depreciated with "excessive" speed.\par \par \uc2 The real rose 1.7 percent to 1.9937 per dollar in its third consecutive session of gains. It was the first time it closed below the level of 2 per dollar since May 14, although it remains nearly 15 percent weaker from a late-February high.\par \par \uc2 Since it resumed the sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps a week ago, this was the first time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered swaps when the real was trading stable against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is willing to make regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid that the real returns to the level of 2.1 per dollar," said Luciano Rostagno, chief strategist at \uc2 WestLB\uc2  bank in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts also said it was too early to say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to draw a line at any specific exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "We can't say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is defending any specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  level yet, as this was the first time it acted like that (when the real was stable)," said Mario Battistel, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  desk manager at Fair brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 "Maybe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was worried about Europe's impact on our market, so it acted early to avoid putting out a fire later."\par \par \uc2 Fears about the impact of a possible Greek exit from the euro zone continued to weigh on global markets, keeping most Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso fell 0.24 percent to 14.0340 per greenback in its fourth consecutive session of losses. A sharp drop of the peso on Wednesday caused the Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to call a dollar auction for the first time since 2009.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso declined 0.12 percent to finish at a fresh 4-1/2-month low of 509.40 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Peru's sol ended practically stable at 2.695 per dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $2 million in the spot market for the first time since October 2011.\par \par \uc2 The Peruvian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been auctioning deposit certificates and repos in recent weeks to satisfy demand for dollars and curb the depreciation of the sol, which has been trading around its weakest levels for 2012.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Rachel Uranga in Mexico City, Ursula Scollo in Peru; Writing by Walter Brandimarte; Editing by Andrea Ricci and Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120528e85p000sd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
