\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico's Peso Closes Stronger Versus Dollar In Upbeat End To 1Q\b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 23:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains 9.2% against dollar in 1Q as euro-zone jitters ease\par \par \uc2 -Improved growth prospects, high oil prices support \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -Further peso gains expected in 2012\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Anthony Harrup \par     Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso closed stronger against the U.S. dollar Friday, ending the quarter on a positive note as investors were encouraged by news on bailout funds for Europe and remained upbeat about economic prospects for the U.S.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso was quoted closing in Mexico City at MXN12.7980 to the dollar, according to Infosel, slightly stronger than its MXN12.8150 close Thursday, and 9.2% stronger than its 2011 close of MXN13.9725.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global investor worries about Europe's precarious debt situation hit all types of risky assets in the final quarter of 2011, carrying the highly liquid peso to its weakest ever year-end close.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The world looks quite a bit different here at the end of the first quarter than it did at the end of last year," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brown Brothers Harriman\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in its second-quarter \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  report. "The combination of stronger U.S. growth and the aggressive liquidity provisions by the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has effectively pushed the global economy away from the abyss that it was facing at the end of 2011."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the emerging markets space, BBH favors Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over Europe, Middle East and Africa, and Asia, where energy importers remain more vulnerable to higher oil prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nomura this week changed its year-end estimate for the peso to MXN12.00 to the dollar from MXN12.80, citing lower risk from Europe, a positive growth outlook, the possibility of Brazilian exchange controls diverting investment flows to Mexico, and still relatively small net long peso positions in futures markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Within Latin America, several analysts see an advantage in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Mexico\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's less \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  attitude toward \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation, as Brazil has already resumed measures to discourage gains in the real.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amid the flurry of volatility late last year, the Bank of Mexico switched its position from a buyer of dollars through monthly put options, to a potential seller via a mechanism under which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will sell from reserves up to $400 million on days when the peso weakens 2% against the dollar. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rebound this year has meant no sales have been triggered, and Bank of Mexico Gov. Agustin Carstens said last month a return to the options mechanism to accumulate more reserves couldn't be ruled out. Exchange-policy decisions are made jointly by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the Finance Ministry.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar revenue from crude oil exports by state monopoly \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleos Mexicanos\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which changes dollars at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is the principal source of reserves, which are currently $148 billion. The peso, therefore, mostly benefits from high crude prices, which also bolster federal budget revenue.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Anthony Harrup, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5980-5176; anthony.harrup@dowjones.com [ 30-03-12 2107GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1027 1852   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120330e83u001cb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
