\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains ahead of ECB cash boost\b0\par\par\uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2012\par 18:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds details)\par \par \uc2 * Brazil's real strengthens past key 1.70 level\par \par \uc2 * Mexico's peso firms 0.37 pct, Brazil gains 0.33 pct\par \par \uc2 By Rachel Uranga\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Feb 28 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened on Tuesday ahead of an expected flood of cheap cash from Europe that could keep Brazil's real beyond the key 1.70 level despite increased \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Europe's banks were expected to guzzle up another half a trillion euros of cheap three-year loans offered by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, according to a Reuters poll of money market traders.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the rock-bottom interest rates on the loans would push banks to use the cash to buy higher-yielding, riskier assets. That is pushing speculators to make the same bets and it could fuel further demand for Latin American debt ahead.\par \par \uc2 "Yields will probably bump lower as a consequence of the liquidity that's being injected," said Enrique Alvarez, Latin America bond and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with IDEAglobal in New York.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real f irmed 0.33 percent to bid at 1.6982 per dollar, breaking past the 1.70 level that market players think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and authorities are defending.\par \par \uc2 A similar liquidity boost from the ECB in December helped fuel a sharp rally in riskier assets during January and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Brazil, Colombia, Chile and Mexico were top gainers among the world's most traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Alfredo Barbutti, an economist at Brazilian brokerage BGC Liquidez, said he expects the real to continue to strengthen if central banks and governments continue easing monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 The real has appreciated more than 9 percent so far this year, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to revive dollar purchases in the spot and derivatives markets to try to slow its advance.\par \par \uc2 "Authorities are very clear, it's a reflection of containment at this time," Alvarez said. "Changing the trend or equalizing the trend is very difficult."\par \par \uc2 After a nearly four-month hiatus Brazil began to buy dollars in the spot market earlier this month, in a bid to protect exporters from strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that undermine their competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian government said on Tuesday it could also use its sovereign wealth fund to buy dollars in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but it would hold off and not interfere in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy.\par \par \uc2 Peru's sol is trading around a 15-year high despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's buying $76 million in the local spot market on Monday.\par \par \uc2 In Colombia, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week extended its dollar buying program though August, the peso has strengthened 0.27 percent to 1767.15 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has gone in the opposite direction to other regional banks raising its interest rates by 25 basis points to 5.25 percent last week in an effort to check inflationary expectations and curb an increase in consumer credit.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time soon. The peso appreciated 0.37 percent to 12.8525 per dollar .\par \par \uc2 Gains in the peso were limited by mixed U.S. data\par \par \uc2 in the United States, Mexico's top trading partner.\par \par \uc2 New orders for U.S. manufactured goods fell in January by the most in three years, suggesting the U.S. economy started the year on a weaker footing than expected.\par \par \uc2 Allaying worries, consumer confidence spiked to a one year high this month according to a private business research group.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso strengthened 0.55 percent to 476.70 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Jean Luis Arce in Mexico City, Peter Murphy in Brasilia and Jos\u233\'00\'E9 de Castro in Sao Paulo)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | U | NAT   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120302e82s00147\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
