\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-EMERGING MARKETS-Chile peso leads Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; Greek debt talks eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2012\par 19:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Refiles to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso extends rally to 6th day on U.S. recovery\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real hits key 1.75/dlr level, triggers profit-taking\par \par \uc2 By Brad Haynes and Rachel Uranga\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Jan 23 (Reuters) - Chile's peso led gains among Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar on Monday on optimism that Greece can avoid a debt default that would drag on global growth.\par \par \uc2 The session's gains may be fleeting, however, as the region's markets closed before news that euro zone finance ministers had rejected an offer made by private bondholders to help restructure Greece's debts.\par \par \uc2 France's foreign minister earlier had said a deal between Greece and its creditors was "taking shape" ahead of a meeting to set the terms of a rescue package for Athens.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso firmed nearly 0.9 percent to 487.9 per U.S. dollar, hitting a four-month high as a rally pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's relative strength index to its most overbought levels seen in a year.\par \par \uc2 "The risk at these levels is profit-taking, but I would see that as a chance to reload," said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, a Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at RBS Securities in Stamford, Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 She said investor flows into Latin America are driving the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength, as moderating concerns about Europe's debt woes drive investment into emerging markets seen benefitting from a global economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso gained 0.23 percent to end at 13.1700 per dollar, gaining for the sixth straight day after economic data last week confirmed a brightening outlook in the United States, which accounts for nearly 80 percent of Mexican export earnings.\par \par \uc2 Francisco Diez, director of emerging market trading at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in New York, said the peso's rally could break 13 per dollar to set a four-month high. Betting on the stronger peso "plays on the strengths of the recovery in the U.S., and (\b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central) bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Diez.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a track record of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real weakened slightly more than 0.4 percent on Monday to trade at 1.7512 per dollar after its recent rise triggered concerns about a policy response.\par \par \uc2 "The 1.75-level has been historically significant for policy \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so local traders are talking up the risk of a (Brazilian) \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move, which prompted some profit-taking," said RBS' Cattan-Naslausky.\par \par \uc2 She noted, however, that an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Brazil seemed unlikely before the exchange rate approaches 1.70 per dollar. Brazilian companies' foreign financing needs and possible equity offerings are supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rally, she added.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Padraic Cassidy, Gary Crosse)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120126e81n0016q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
