\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Peso Defense Opens Path For Mexico Rate Cuts: \uc2 BBVA\b0\par\par\uc2 135 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2011\par 19:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1:47 (Dow Jones) Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the peso is part of a broader strategy that should pave the way for monetary easing, says \uc2 BBVA\uc2  chief fixed-income strategist Ociel Hernandez. Peso depreciation is the main factor limiting the Bank of Mexico's easing intent, he says, but \uc2 BBVA\uc2  expects \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness will be contained by the decision to sell dollars if the peso weakens 2% in a single day. \uc2 BBVA\uc2  maintains the view that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will lower interest rates by 50 basis points between January and March of next year. (juan.montes@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at 212.416.3100 or email paul.vigna@dowjones.com [ 12-15-11 1347ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020111215e7cf000k7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
