\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico's Peso Closes Flat On The Day, Up On The Week Vs Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2011\par 22:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now 4.6% stronger than it was a week ago\par \par \uc2 --Peso appreciates after Mexican authorities say they will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets\par \par \uc2 --The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaves interest rates unchanged at 4.5%\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Juan Montes \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's peso closed nearly flat Friday against the U.S. dollar, concluding a positive week in which improved sentiment about the European debt situation, and planned \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Mexico\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb sharp swings in the exchange rate, lent support to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso was quoted closing in Mexico City at MXN13.5925 to the dollar, compared with MXN13.60 Thursday and 4.6% stronger than it was a week ago.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investor doubts about the future of the euro and prospects for some euro-zone countries have made the peso a lightning rod for risk aversion, since it is one of the most-traded emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Investors also have been hedging their exposure to Mexican securities through the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  futures market, contributing to the peso's recent decline to its weakest level since March 2009.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Tuesday, the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  commission announced that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will sell up to $400 million on days the peso is 2% weaker than the previous session, and also said it would halt its monthly dollar put options, which it had conducted as a means of accumulating foreign reserves by buying dollars when the peso was appreciating.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The exchange rate is continuing its downward trend ahead of a possible dollar selling period by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said brokerage Actinver in a note, adding that the support level is MXN13.50.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Friday, the Bank of Mexico left its policy interest rate unchanged at 4.5%, in line with analyst expectations. The Mexican \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said economic growth risks have deteriorated and a rate cut couldn't be dismissed in the future, but also highlighted that weakness and volatility in the peso remain a key risk for inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Consistent with Bank of Mexico not changing its tone, the market's reaction to the statement has been fairly muted," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts. "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to show a neutral stance, with no urgency to start easing."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Juan Montes, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5980 5178; juan.montes@dowjones.com [ 02-12-11 2139GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1027 1852   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111202e7c20011i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
