\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Mexico  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  moves to defend peso\b0\par\par\uc2 885 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2011\par 21:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Mexico \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps up support for peso\par \par \uc2 * To offer $400 million on days of big peso drops\par \par \uc2 * Analysts say move could support later rate cut\par \par \uc2 (Adds quote from official, paragraphs 3-4)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Nov 29 (Reuters) - Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to defend the peso on Tuesday as a slump in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks fanning inflation and driving investors from the country's bond market.\par \par \uc2 In its most forceful move to protect the peso since the collapse of U.S. investment bank \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  during the 2008 financial crisis, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would restart daily market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on days of huge peso losses.\par \par \uc2 "A volatile international environment can provoke major swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , more so than local conditions," said Mexico's deputy finance minister Gerardo Rodriguez, who sits on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  commission that sets policy for the peso.\par \par \uc2 "These abrupt fluctuations are what we are trying to avoid with the measures taken by the commission," Rodriguez told local radio.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the decision by perhaps Latin America's most orthodox supporters of free markets suggested policy-makers are concerned that Europe's debt crisis could explode into a global financial panic similar to 2008.\par \par \uc2 "They are being pre-emptive here, given how fluid the external situation remains," said Roberto Melzi, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> surged nearly 1.5 percent on the news, rising to 13.8250 per dollar after trading past 14 per dollar earlier in the session.\par \par \uc2 Market players have been eyeing the potential for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the peso broke past 14 per dollar to a 2-1/2-year low last week.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 For an INSTANT VIEW from analysts: [ID:nN1E7AS1R4]\par \par \uc2 For a CHRONOLOGY on peso \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 : [ID:nN1E7AS1O9]\par \par \uc2 For a FACTBOX on \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk: [ID:nRISKMX]\par \par \uc2 Story on Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  [ID:nN1E7AS1QO]\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's last round of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was triggered in October 2008 when the peso dropped 6 percent in a single day to hit its lowest level in 16 years amid tight liquidity conditions.\par \par \uc2 Still, the current threat of action falls short of the nearly $11 billion the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctioned up front in October 2008. Daily dollar auctions were only suspended in April last year.\par \par \uc2 The risk that a weak peso could drive up inflation pushed investors to call off bets of an interest-rate cut this Friday. All 19 analysts in a Reuters poll expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board to keep rates on hold on Friday. [ID:nWNA4305]\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  economist Gabriel Casillas said if the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanism succeeded in stabilizing the peso, it could give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cover to eventually cut its benchmark rate from the current 4.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 "This could set the conditions for a rate cut in the future," he said.\par \par \uc2 AUCTION MECHANISM\par \par \uc2 On days when the peso is buffeted by big market moves of more than 2 percent in a single session, the bank will offer up $400 million daily in a bid to shield the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from global turmoil.\par \par \uc2 The peso has fallen 2 percent in a full day's trade about eight times since volatility spiked in August. While the $400 million is only a fraction of the amount traded daily in Latin America's most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some analysts said the signal was key and suggested more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could follow.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also suspended a monthly sale of dollar put options aimed at preventing the peso from appreciating, a mechanism that has helped boost foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to $140 billion.\par \par \uc2 A slump of more than 16 percent in the peso since August has fanned concerns that higher import prices could feed into inflation, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said this could be one hurdle in cutting interest rates to support a still weak economy.\par \par \uc2 "What is happening is that the exchange rate has depreciated a lot and very fast," said \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  economist Fernando Losada. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to prevent a contamination of the exchange rate into domestic prices."\par \par \uc2 Other central banks have taken a more hands-on approach to sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves in the past, slapping on capital controls and directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets.\par \par \uc2 But Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Agustin Carstens is generally loath to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets, and analysts say he would probably not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's discretion unless liquidity considerations deteriorated significantly. [ID:nN31220972]\par \par \uc2 The move to set the framework for limited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should offer bondholders some insurance against further losses that could push them to abandon Mexican debt. Foreign investors hold a record amount of longer-term Mexican debt, worth around $50 billion.\par \par \uc2 More \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses could force investors to dump bonds, which would further hurt the peso, and push more investors to sell bonds in a deepening spiral of losses.\par \par \uc2 "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to exaggerate and overshoot, it would create huge deleveraging risk," said Siobhan Morden, head of Latin America strategy at RBS Securities in Stamford, Connecticut. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Lorena Segura, Noe Torres and Luis Rojas Mena in Mexico City and Walter Brandimarte in New York; Editing by Jan Paschal, Gary Hill)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 4)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111202e7bt001gm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
