\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Bank Of Mexico To Sell Dollars On Days Peso Weakens 2%\b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2011\par 22:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Bank of Mexico to sell as much as $400 million a day when peso is 2% weaker\par \par \uc2 --Monthly dollar put options suspended until further notice\par \par \uc2 --Peso, government bonds rally on decision\par \par \uc2 (Updates with details of previous auctions, level of foreign reserves, market reaction)\par \par \uc2 By Anthony Harrup\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  commission said Tuesday that the Bank of Mexico will sell as much as $400 million a day in the exchange market on days when the peso is 2% weaker than the previous session, and that it will suspend its monthly auctions of dollar put options under which the bank had been buying dollars.\par \par \uc2 The decision to reinstate the conditional dollar sales, which were used in previous crises, comes after the peso recently fell to its weakest level against the U.S. dollar since March 2009, largely as a result of risk aversion brought on by the debt crisis in Europe.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  commission, formed by the Bank of Mexico and the Finance Ministry, said in a statement that the sale of dollars is intended to maintain orderly functioning of the exchange market and provide liquidity when needed, given current conditions in the international financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Beginning Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will auction $400 million a day at a minimum price that is 2% above the previous day's exchange rate, so that dollars will only be sold when the peso is at least 2% weaker from the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Mexico is also suspending the sale of dollar put options under which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would buy up to $600 million a month. The put options, which were used to bolster foreign reserves, were exercisable on days when the peso was stronger against the dollar than its 20-day average. None of the $600 million in options for November have been exercised, and Wednesday's auction of options for December was canceled.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's foreign reserves stood at $139.6 billion at the end of last week, close to record levels. Mexico also has an unused $72 billion flexible credit line with the International Monetary Fund.\par \par \uc2 The peso rallied sharply on news of the planned \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and was quoted in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City at MXN13.7655 around 4 p.m. EST, according to Infosel, compared with MXN14.0530 at the close Monday.\par \par \uc2 Government bonds also gained, pushing yields lower. The yield on benchmark 10-year bonds was down 15 basis points to 6.49%, and the yield on 20-year bonds was off 12 basis points at 7.59%. Local bonds have been largely unscathed by the recent bouts of global risk aversion, with several analysts saying that foreign investors, rather than selling, have been hedging the risk through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures, leading to net short peso positions in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 The last time that the Bank of Mexico sold dollars in the exchange market was during the 2008-2009 global financial crisis. Between October 2008 and October 2009, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold more than $30 billion through direct auctions, conditional auctions with the 2% rule, and occasional unannounced direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curtail speculation. The conditional auctions were gradually lowered from $400 million to $250 million, and suspended in April 2010.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Harrup, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5980-5176;\par \par \uc2 anthony.harrup@dowjones.com [ 29-11-11 2128GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111129e7bt0017v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
