\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-POLL-Mexico peso seen firming nearly 4 pct by year end\b0\par\par\uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2011\par 22:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso seen trading at 12.96/dlr by end 2011\par \par \uc2 * Stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could back bets for a rate cut\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if peso weakens to 14.50/dlr\par \par \uc2 (Recasts; adds comments, background)\par \par \uc2 By Jean Luis Arce and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Oct 19 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso will firm nearly 4 percent by the end of the year, according to the median of a Reuters poll, which analysts said could give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more room to cut interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso slumped about 11 percent in September in its worst month since the 2008 financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the peso would likely firm from current levels if Europe can contain fears about its debt crisis and if data suggests United States, Mexico's top trading partner, will skirt another recession.\par \par \uc2 The median expectation of 26 analysts surveyed by Reuters is for the peso <MXN=> to trade at 12.96 per dollar by the end of 2011, compared to current levels around 13.46.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signaled last Friday it was prepared to cut interest rates if the global economy worsens but a further fall in the peso could be a stumbling block, since higher import prices may stoke inflation. [ID:nN1E79C25Y]\par \par \uc2 "To the degree that the peso appreciates, the chance of a cut is going to be much higher," said Gabriel Casillas, an economist at \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Benchmark Mexican credit costs have been at 4.5 percent since mid-2009.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Interactive graphic on economies in the Americas:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/nem92s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/nem92s}}}\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  AT 14.50/DLR\par \par \uc2 Mexican inflation is hovering just above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target rate of 3 percent but prolonged weakness in the peso could worry policymakers. [ID:nWNA1278]\par \par \uc2 Bets on Mexican interest rate swaps see a nearly two-in-three chance for a 25 basis point cut by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in December and the market has fully priced in such a cut by January. <BOMWATCH2>\par \par \uc2 By the close of 2012, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen trading at 12.70 per dollar, or 6 percent stronger from current levels, according to the median of 22 analysts.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , led by perhaps the most orthodox supporters of free markets in Latin America, is seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to support the peso if it weakens to 14.50 per dollar, according to the median of 18 analysts.\par \par \uc2 However, many analysts refused to name a specific level for when authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only wade into markets to defend the peso in the case of an extremely quick depreciation that was accompanied by big outflows from the local bond market in conditions of distressed liquidity. [ID:nN1E79D130]\par \par \uc2 "It is all about the velocity of the depreciation and if there are outflows or not, not so much the level," said Salvador Orozco, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Santander in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City.\par \par \uc2 The last round of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was triggered by a 6 percent drop in the peso in a single day to its lowest in 16 years, amid the market turmoil of October 2008.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Noe Torres; Editing by Diane Craft)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-MEXICO/ (UPDATE 1, POLL)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111022e7aj000lw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
