\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso up on Bernanke, Chile peso slumps\b0\par\par\uc2 606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2011\par 20:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Bernanke keeps hopes alive of further Fed stimulus\par \par \uc2 * Euro-zone worries seen keeping pressure on Latam \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso hits 14-month low on copper's rout\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Jean Luis Arce\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Oct 4 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso gained on Tuesday after the head of the U.S. Federal Reserve raised hopes of more economic stimulus, but Chile's peso slid to a 14-month low on a rout in copper prices.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso advanced and U.S. stocks cut losses after Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to act further to help the economy of the United States, which is Mexico's top trading partner. [ID:nW1E7KM007]\par \par \uc2 "The signal that the Fed could take more action down the line is what gave markets a bit of a boost," said Alejandro Padilla, an analyst at Banorte-Ixe in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=><MXN=D2> rose 0.77 percent to 13.96 per dollar. Four straight sessions of steep losses had taken it within striking distance of a more than two-year low.\par \par \uc2 But analysts said the peso and Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would remain vulnerable to more losses. The euro zone's debt troubles will likely push investors to keep dumping riskier assets, such as emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "In the medium term, the issue of Europe is going to keep weighing. There is clearly the worry about whether Greece will be able to meet its obligations," Padilla said.\par \par \uc2 European finance ministers are considering making banks take bigger losses on Greek debt and have postponed a vital aid payment to Athens until mid-November, setting up a moment of truth in the euro zone's sovereign debt crisis. [ID:nL5E7L419D]\par \par \uc2 Investors fear another financial crisis could further drag down global growth just as the U.S. and European economies are already slowing down.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real <BRBY> bid 0.18 percent firmer at 1.8870 per dollar, helped by an auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts that mimic the purchase of dollars in the futures market and provide investors with insurance against declines in the value of the real. [ID:nN1E7930UT]\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to bolster the real, and some analysts think authorities could step up efforts to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it breaks 1.90 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real has slumped about 18 percent since late July. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was undercut in August after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a surprise move to cut interest rates, curbing the appeal of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to yield-hungry investors.\par \par \uc2 Expectations that Brazil could further relax monetary policy are sapping support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The real had been a favorite bet for emerging market investors due to the country's high interest rates for much of the recovery from the 2008 financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Mexican authorities have recently suggested they will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the peso. \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso has shed around 16 percent since late July.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso <CLP=CL> shed 1.8 percent to bid at 534.70 per dollar as prices for copper, the country's main export, continued to slump, also trading near a 14-month low\par \par \uc2 "There is no recovery in copper, so there will be no respite for the peso," said Daniel Soto, an analyst at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso has lost 17 percent since late July.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Froilan Romero in Santiago; Editing by Jan Paschal)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111007e7a4001db\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
