\par\par \b \uc2 Mexican Peso Stumbles On Greek Worries, Near 2.5-Year Low Again\b0\par\par\uc2 416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2011\par 22:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --MXN falls 0.9% against USD on Greece concerns\par \par \uc2 --Carstens downplays role of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --Remittances rise, but economists see Mexican economy cooling\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Amy Guthrie \par     Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MEXICO CITY (Dow Jones)--The Mexican peso fell against the U.S. dollar Monday, finishing the session on the cusp of its key MXN14 psychological level, as concerns resurfaced about Greece's ability to make debt payments.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Infosel quoted the peso closing at MXN13.9945 to the U.S. dollar, once again hovering near a 2 1/2-year low and 0.9% weaker than its close Friday of MXN13.8735.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Greek government said Sunday that it will miss its deficit targets this year, splashing doubt onto whether the European Union will dispense aid in time and driving investors away from risky global assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Mexico Monday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Agustin Carstens downplayed the benefits of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying that what will ultimately elevate the Mexican \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is solid economic fundamentals.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Mexico\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stopped \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in pursuit of a certain exchange rate many years ago," Carstens said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The "sporadic" \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that the bank has undertaken, Carstens said, have occurred with one fundamental objective in common: to guarantee the orderly function of the market while avoiding illiquid conditions that could lead to "excessive volatility" in the exchange rate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Carstens said he expects that Mexico's economic fundamentals will anchor the peso at stronger levels in the medium-term.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In local economic news, remittances from Mexicans living abroad rose 9.2% in August from the year-ago month, to $2.13 billion, bringing remittances for the first eight months of the year to $15.19 billion, a 4.9% increase.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yet the peso's recent tumble led economists surveyed in September by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lower their year-end forecast to MXN12.62 from MXN12.12 in the August survey.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The average estimate for 2011 growth in gross domestic product was 3.8%, while the estimate for 2012 fell to 3.5% from 3.6% in August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Mexico's link with the U.S. has meant that the slowdown is well underway," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  wrote in a note, saying that evidence that the Mexican economy is cooling will likely motivate the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ease monetary policy by year-end.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Amy Guthrie, Dow Jones Newswires; (5255) 5980-5177; amy.guthrie@dowjones.com [ 03-10-11 2050GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1027 1852   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111003e7a30017r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
