\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Bank Of Mexico Deputy Governor: Euro-Zone Situation 'Main Concern'\b0\par\par\uc2 537 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2011\par 17:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 14 Jul 2011 11:11 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Mexico Deputy Gov: Tighter Policy Possible Without Rate Hike\par \par \uc2 14 Jul 2011 11:11 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Mexico Deputy Governor: Euro-Zone Situation 'Main Concern'\par \par \uc2 14 Jul 2011 11:12 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Mexico Deputy Gov: Tighter Policy Possible Without Rate Hike\par \par \uc2 14 Jul 2011 11:14 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Mexico Deputy Gov: Recent US Data A Concern\par \par \uc2 14 Jul 2011 11:15 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Mexico Deputy Gov: Recent US Data A Concern\par \par \uc2 14 Jul 2011 11:15 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Mexico Deputy Gov: Peso Strength Helps Fight Inflation\par \par \uc2 14 Jul 2011 11:16 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Mexico Deputy Gov: Peso Strength Helps Fight Inflation\par \par \uc2 14 Jul 2011 11:18 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Mexico Deputy Gov: Monitoring Foreign Banks Closely\par \par \uc2 14 Jul 2011 11:19 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Mexico Deputy Gov: Monitoring Foreign Banks Closely\par \par \uc2 14 Jul 2011 11:20 EDT *DJ  Bank Of Mexico Deputy Gov: Don't See Concerns About Peso Strength\par \par \uc2 14 Jul 2011 12:37 EDT DJ  Bank Of Mexico: Monetary Policy Could Tighten Without Rate Increase\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Erin McCarthy \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Tighter monetary policy in Mexico may be possible without raising interest rates thanks to benign inflation, Bar/nk of Mexico Deputy Governor Manuel Sanchez said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since the U.S.'s monetary policy is relatively accommodative, it makes Mexico's rate relatively more restrictive, which helps control inflation, Sanchez said in an interview with Dow Jones Newswires. "We don't have to move because inflation is coming down, and actually, now our monetary policy stance may be gradually looking a little tighter because inflation is coming down without moving anything."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Mexico left its overnight interest rate target unchanged at 4.5% last week. The bank has held the rate at that level for two years, and is widely expected to stay on hold until the second quarter of 2012.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This is primarily because inflationary pressures continue to be tame in Mexico, with consumer prices unchanged in June and annual inflation standing at 3.28%. Annual core inflation was at 3.18% last month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  maintains an inflation target of 3%, plus or minus one percentage point.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Mexican peso's appreciation is also helping to keep inflation in check, Sanchez added. The peso has strengthened about 5% against the dollar since the beginning of 2011, according to CQG.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Though other regional central banks have taken steps to curb their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' appreciation, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Mexico\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is known for a less \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  buys up to $600 million a month via a system of put options that can be exercised when the peso is stronger than its 20-day average. Under the options, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  takes advantage of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength to bolster foreign reserves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sanchez said he doesn't see concern about the peso's strength, especially because Mexican exports continue to perform well.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 14, 2011 12:37 ET (16:37 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110714e77e004io\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
