\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexico peso, Brazil real up; Chile peso slumps\b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 17:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Japan disaster keeps investors cautious\par \par \uc2 * Chile rate hikes seen backstopping peso losses\par \par \uc2 * Brazil seen preparing more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real firms 0.24 percent, \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso 0.11 pct\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, March 14 (Reuters) - Mexico peso and Brazil's real firmed on Monday as investors bet neither Japan's disaster nor oil prices will have a big enough impact on global growth to deter demand for Latin America's high-yielding debt.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso shook off losses to firm past 11.90 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at its strongest level since October 2008 during the session.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked a recovery from session lows in U.S. stocks markets as investors bet the broad impact on equities from Japan's disaster may be short-lived.\par \par \uc2 "People seem to be thinking the reaction to the Japan disaster was overdone," said Dirk Willer, head of Latin American local markets strategy at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 A catastrophe at one of Japan's nuclear power plants that was damaged in the earthquake could spur more losses, Willer said. "But if they get the reactors under control, the flooding and the earthquake itself will lead to a reconstruction boom, and that might, if anything, be seen as positive for global growth," he added.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> firmed 0.11 percent to 11.8950 per dollar while Brazil's real <BRBY> firmed 0.24 percent to 1.660 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brazil is offering some of the highest interest rates in the world, bolstering demand for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The market awaited news of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures from Brazilian authorities, who want to keep in check the real's gains that are hurting local manufacturers by cheapening imports.[ID:nN14145427]\par \par \uc2 However, any new measures may not be able to spur more than short-term losses in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has advanced more than 40 percent since 2009. Increasing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has slowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains, but has not reversed its advance.\par \par \uc2 Unrest in North Africa and the Middle East has put pressure on oil prices, but analysts said that the cost of crude would have to rise much higher for a sustained period to take a major toll on global growth and derail the stability of the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso is seen getting further support from signs of an improving local economy that is tracking the recovery in the United States, Mexico's top trading partner.\par \par \uc2 Data showed Mexican industrial production rose at its fastest pace in 15 months as manufacturing output jumped and the construction sector posted a big increase. [ID:nN14143186].\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso <CLP=CL> lost 0.52 percent to 481 per dollar. Chile's local spot market closed before U.S. stocks pared losses.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said expectations of further interest rate hikes could limit losses in the Chilean peso this week.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen raising its benchmark interest rate by 25 basis points to 3.75 percent this Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Chile is still hiking and could hike more than what is priced in; you would have to have a very negative shock on the global growth outlook for this to change," said Roberto Melzi, a strategist at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110317e73e001bo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
