\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  firm; Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 18:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects last paragraph to show Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars, not selling)\par \par \uc2 * Euro bounce supports bids for emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Market awaits possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures in Brazil\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso up 0.23 pct, Chile peso firms 0.11 pct\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, March 9 (Reuters) - The Mexican and Chilean pesos firmed on Wednesday as a stronger euro backed bids for riskier assets, but further gains could be limited by uncertainty related to Europe's debt troubles and rising oil prices.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, investors awaited possible news of fresh government measures to tame gains in the Brazilian real when local markets reopen this afternoon following Carnival holidays.\par \par \uc2 The euro recovered from lows on Wednesday after Portugal successfully sold bonds, easing some concerns about European countries struggling with high debt burdens. [ID:nN09244748]\par \par \uc2 The euro is often a proxy for investor appetite for riskier assets such as emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Mexican peso tracked the euro's bounce.\par \par \uc2 "We have seen a rebound in the euro, which has set a better tone for risky assets, so emerging markets are benefiting from that," said Jorge Perez-Duarte, a managing director at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2  in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso <MXN=> firmed 0.23 percent to 11.9775 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has struggled to definitively break past the 12 per dollar level since a rally stalled in late January.\par \par \uc2 "The peso does not have much more room to go, the outlook on Europe really is mixed," said Antonio Magana, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at brokerage Interacciones in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 The cost of dollars in pesos would have to fall below a 2-1/2 year low hit in January at 11.9439 to open up the field for a significant break lower, Perez-Duarte said.\par \par \uc2 Worries about high oil prices could also begin to weigh on markets again and unravel peso gains, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <CLP=CL> firmed 0.11 percent to 474.50 per dollar on rising prices for copper, the country's main export.\par \par \uc2 However, higher oil prices could keep investors worried that inflationary pressures may hit economic growth and demand for copper.\par \par \uc2 Global markets are expected to remain jittery among concerns that political unrest in Egypt and Libya could spread to other oil states such as top producer Saudi Arabia.\par \par \uc2 PARTY'S OVER\par \par \uc2 With the end of Brazil's Carnival holiday, local authorities may move soon to try and sober up investors who pushed the real to a 2-1/2 year high last Friday, beyond what many see as the finance ministry's unofficial limit.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's financial markets reopen at 1 p.m. local time (1600 GMT). A Finance Ministry source told Reuters the government may announce a new round of measures this week. [ID:nN04241800]\par \par \uc2 The real closed at 1.645 per dollar on Friday in the local spot market, below the 1.65 per dollar level that has been seen as a trigger to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures in the past.\par \par \uc2 Testing government resolve, the real bid stronger at 1.6443 in international trade <BRL=> on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has steadily escalated its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since 2009 as a tide of global investment was drawn to its double-digit interest rates. The flows pumped up the real by more than 40 percent since the beginning of 2009.\par \par \uc2 The stronger real is hurting local manufacturers who have to compete with cheapening imports.\par \par \uc2 So far, Brazil's efforts to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  have slowed, but not deterred its advance.\par \par \uc2 Last October, the government tripled to 6 percent a tax on foreigners buying local bonds and trading in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivatives. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, is buying dollars in the spot market as well as acting in the forward and swap markets.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by W Simon)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CORRECTED)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110312e739000kt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
