\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile peso firms as data backs bigger rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 599 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 16:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chile data supports bets of 50 bps hike next week\par \par \uc2 * Higher oil prices contain gains\par \par \uc2 * Further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures expected in Brazil\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso firms 0.14 pct, Chile peso 0.23 pct\par \par \uc2 By Moises Avila and Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO/MEXICO CITY, March 7 (Reuters) - Strong economic growth data out of Chile on Monday boosted the peso as it backed bets of a steeper interest rate hike next week, while Mexico's peso nudged below the key 12-per-dollar level.\par \par \uc2 A broadly weaker U.S. dollar supported bids for the region's assets. Investors are betting the U.S. Federal Reserve will lag Europe in raising interest rates. Brazil and Chile are already hiking rates, pushing up yields on their debt.\par \par \uc2 Data showing Chile's economy grew 1.3 percent in January compared with December backed bets that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step up the pace of its recent interest rate hikes to 50 basis points in its next policy decision on March 17.\par \par \uc2 "The data was was better than expected, too much better," said Sergio Tricio, head of research at \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile. "The data is clearly firming the peso," he added.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso <CLP=CL> bid 0.23 percent stronger at 472.60 per dollar. The head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen taking a stronger tone in a speech last Friday in comments on the need to attack the threat of rising inflation.\par \par \uc2 Global investors are expected to keep pumping up Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Since U.S. interest rates are seen on hold until next year, market players can borrow in dollars, invest in Latin American debt, and pocket the difference between interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Tricio warned that a push higher by oil prices could erode support for the Chilean peso. Chile imports most of its oil and demand for copper, the country's main export, could be damaged if higher crude prices weigh down global economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> firmed 0.14 percent to 11.9880 per dollar. The peso has struggled since late January to definitively break past the 12 per dollar level.\par \par \uc2 Investors worry that rising oil prices could hit the U.S. consumer, who buys most of Mexico's exports. Those fears derailed a peso rally that began last November, leaving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade in a range.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude rose to $118 a barrel and U.S. oil hit the highest since September 2008 on Monday as fighting in Libya disrupted its supplies and renewed concern of wider disruptions in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 "Conflicts will have to subside to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  advance toward 11.90/11.92," said Alfredo Puig, a trader at brokerage Vector in Monterrey.\par \par \uc2 The local spot market in Brazil was closed for Carnival, but in international trade the real rebounded <BRL=> from a 2-1/2 year high hit on Friday.\par \par \uc2 A source at the Finance Ministry told Reuters the government could introduce new measures later this week to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains, which are hurting local exporters. [ID:nN04241800]\par \par \uc2 In international trade, the real was 0.7 percent weaker from its close on the local spot market, trading around 1.6547 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has used a barrage of measures to curb the real, considered one of the world's most overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The country offers interest rates that are among the world's highest, and last week policymakers raised their benchmark rate to 11.75 percent with further increases expected.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110310e73700199\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
