\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso sinks;  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears hit Chile\b0\par\par\uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2011\par 15:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurt by concerns of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumps, heavy positioning weighs\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso slumps 1 pct, Brazil real 0.06 pct\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Froilan Romero\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SANTIAGO, Feb 15 (Reuters) - Chile's peso slumped by the most in six weeks on Tuesday on falling copper prices and bets authorities may try to limit speculative inflows, while Mexico's peso sank to a two-week low.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso slipped back from a six-week high as prices for copper, the country's main export, retreated from a record high. Rising inflation in top copper consumer China raised concerns that tighter borrowing costs there that could hit global demand. [ID:nLDE71E21N]\par \par \uc2 Traders also cited growing speculation that the government could try again to contain the peso's gains, which are hurting local exporters.\par \par \uc2 "Banks are taking long-dollar positions to protect themselves from an eventual announcement of measures to brake the peso's gains, this time it could come from the finance ministry," said a trader in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=CL> shed 0.6 percent to 472.30 pesos.\par \par \uc2 The peso lost ground for the first time in five sessions after surging on bets that Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise its benchmark interest rate this week.[ID:nN14110508]\par \par \uc2 Expectations of higher interest rates had helped the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firm back close to a nearly three-year high and erase most of its losses since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveiled an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program at the beginning of January.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not expected to boost its daily dollar purchase program, but the finance ministry could move to tax foreign inflows or it could change regulations governing the market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of local pension funds, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> sank 1 percent to 12.17 per dollar, on track to post its biggest one-day loss since violent protests in Egypt rattled global markets at the end of January.\par \par \uc2 The peso began to weaken after a report on January U.S. retail sales showed they grew less than expected. Mexico sends most of its exports to the United States and it is depending on U.S. demand to fuel economic growth this year.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso weakened past its 20-day moving average, pushing some traders to dump the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which then pushed it through other investors' stop-loss levels, deepening the peso's slide.\par \par \uc2 "There is a complete lack of conviction out there, some people are taking risk off the table and Mexico is vulnerable because everyone is so long," said Paul Biszko, a senior emerging markets strategist at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso has by far the most speculative bets in its favor - or long positions - among the eight major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracked by Reuters. [ID:nN11301566]\par \par \uc2 Before Tuesday's losses, the Mexican peso gained more than 4 percent since November on the back of a better outlook for the economy of the United States, Mexico's main trading partner.\par \par \uc2 But the heavy bias in favor of the peso can end up hurting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when unforeseen losses, such as Tuesday's, push speculators to run for the door.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real <BRBY> bid 0.06 percent weaker at 1.668 per dollar, likely supported by IPO-related flows into the markets, Biszko noted.\par \par \uc2 The real's strength would probably be limited by continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, traders said, as Latin America's top economy seeks to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains that make its exports less competitive.\par \par \uc2 Yields on Brazilian interest rate futures contracts <0#DIJ:> edged lower after local retail sales volumes stayed unexpectedly flat in December and investors pared their bets for a cycle of interest rate hikes. Brazil's retail sales were expected to rise 0.6 percent, according to Reuters poll. (Additional reporting by Moises Avila in Santiago, Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|E|U|RBN|D|M|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110218e72f00124\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
