\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile peso hits 6-wk high, Brazil yields jump\b0\par\par\uc2 689 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2011\par 15:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chile peso boosted by copper prices, rate hike bets\par \par \uc2 * Brazil yields rise after jump in inflation expectations\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real dips 0.12 pct, Mexico peso 0.15 pct (Updates prices, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Moises Avila and Silvio Cascione\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO/SAO PAULO, Feb 14 (Reuters) - Chile's peso hit a six-week high on Monday amid higher copper prices and bets of an interest rate hike this week, while yields on Brazilian rate futures shot up on rising inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 Prices for copper, Chile's main export, rallied to a fresh record high on Monday following data showing a surge in China's copper imports. For details, see [ID:nLDE71D0PP]\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen raising its benchmark rate to 3.50 percent this week, resuming hikes after a pause last month partly to avoid further appreciation in the peso.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, the market has ruled out an increase in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $50 million-a-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program for the time being after the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested last week that inflation concerns will drive monetary policy, not concerns about the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "Besides the increase in copper prices, the market continues to bet on a stronger peso after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Jose De Gregorio said the bank will focus more on controlling inflationary pressures," said Bci analyst Osvaldo Cruz.\par \par \uc2 "The market is also betting on the bank increasing its benchmark rate and that could affect the (exchange) rate."\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso <CLP=> firmed 0.6 percent to 469.40 per dollar, strengthening below the key resistance level of 470. It is now within striking distance of the 465.50 per dollar level that triggered the launch of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program last month to protect exporters from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strong gains. [ID:nN30113748]\par \par \uc2 Traders see the peso's next resistance level at 468 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL RATES\par \par \uc2 Yields on Brazilian interest rate futures <0#DIJ:> shot up after economists jacked up inflation expectations for 2011, despite government promises last week for a $30 billion budget cut meant to ease price pressures. [ID:nN14119393]\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is struggling to keep the economy from overheating. Some investors are betting that policymakers are not taking strong enough action to control inflation. In January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked its benchmark lending rate by 50 basis points to 11.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 "We suspect it will take bolder policy action before inflation expectations improve much," \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  analysts said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 The yield on the rate contract due January 2012 <DIJF2> rose from 12.33 percent to 12.43 percent after the inflation survey.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real <BRBY> was bid 0.12 percent weaker to 1.667 in the local spot market, continuing its recent tendency to trade in a narrow range. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at two auctions in a bid to contain its strength\par \par \uc2 Government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to curb the real's strength have put a cap on gains below 1.65 reais per dollar, for the time being, but flows continue to seek out investments in local bonds, which offer among the world's highest interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "There are still investments entering Brazil," said Marcos Marcos Trabbold, a trader at brokerage B&T Corretora de Cambio. "But without a doubt, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are keeping the dollar in a range," he added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso <MXN=> weakened 0.15 percent to 12.05 per dollar. Mexico's peso has been unable to definitively break past the 12-per-dollar level since firming below the key benchmark last month for the first time since October 2008.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said renewed speculation that the government could boost the amount of dollar put options it is selling every month to accumulate reserves is helping keep the peso in check.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's dollar option auctions are seen as a less aggressive form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  being used by other central banks in the region like Chile and Brazil.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110217e72e0013s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
