\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  finance minister rules out  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2011\par 16:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  respects rules of free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime\par \par \uc2 * Peso hasn't risen as much as some Latam \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Mexico's export strength doesn't require weaker peso\par \par \uc2 * Finance Ministry could revise up Mexico 2011 growth view (Adds details on growth forecast, background)\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Feb 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb the appreciation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Finance Minister Ernesto Cordero said on Thursday, brushing off complaints from exporters who want a weaker peso.\par \par \uc2 Unlike other emerging market countries, Mexico has seen only modest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains in the past few months, Cordero told a housing conference in New York. He noted that the peso is still weaker than pre-crisis levels.\par \par \uc2 "In Mexico, we respect the rules of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. We do not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in it and we will remain like that," he told reporters after a presentation to investors.\par \par \uc2 "It's very difficult to determine the equilibrium price of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Cordero said.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been on the sidelines of the so-called \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war that has pushed many emerging market countries to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in order to protect their exports from local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Cordero dismissed complaints from some Mexican exporters, who want a weaker peso to better compete with Chinese products in the United States, Mexico's top trading partner.\par \par \uc2 "Mexico's exporting strength does not depend on our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It depends on the human capital that we have, our geographic position, lower costs of transport and our logistic platform," he said.\par \par \uc2 Cordero also said inflation is under control in Mexico even as growth accelerates. He said the Finance Ministry will likely revise its current 2011 growth forecast of 4.0 percent, which he called "conservative."\par \par \uc2 "Probably the same story that happened in 2010 is going to repeat and we'll be improving that forecast in Mexico," he added.\par \par \uc2 MEXICO-ECONOMY/CORDERO (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110210e72a001wq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
