\par\par \b \uc2 HIGHLIGHTS-Mexico sees lower inflation, strong growth\b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2011\par 21:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Feb 9 (Reuters) - Mexico's inflation rate will be lower in 2011 than last year and the country's economy is likely to show strong growth this year and next, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Agustin Carstens said on Wednesday. [nN09172638]\par \par \uc2 Below are highlights of his comments at the presentation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quarterly inflation report.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FX INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 "You can't depend on exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , firstly because the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for its own pleasure."\par \par \uc2 "The message to the country's business leaders is that the Bank of Mexico will continue with its prime mandate of beating inflation ... and that medium- to long-term competitiveness can only be gained through greater public and private spending."\par \par \uc2 NO LABOR PRESSURES\par \par \uc2 "The salary base is growing, but from the point of view of inflation ... we don't see pressures."\par \par \uc2 CAPITAL FLOWS\par \par \uc2 "We cannot rule out more \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility due to a reversal in capital flows."\par \par \uc2 MEXICAN INFLATION\par \par \uc2 "Our objective is 3 percent and our margin does not reflect a comfort zone."\par \par \uc2 "For 2011 ... we expect to see levels below the inflation we saw in 2010."\par \par \uc2 "Looking at inflation expectations to the close of 2011, they are again quite well behaved, I reiterate, above 3 percent."\par \par \uc2 PESO STRENGTH\par \par \uc2 "The national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength has cushioned the impact of rising prices abroad."\par \par \uc2 ECONOMIC GROWTH\par \par \uc2 "We've got to be very clear ... Mexico's economic fundamentals remain solid."\par \par \uc2 "Exports continue to be an important growth factor." (Reporting by Mexico Newsroom)\par \par \uc2 MEXICO-ECONOMY/ (HIGHLIGHTS)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110209e729001nq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
